    "file_name": "AFP_ENG_19970407.0311.tml",
    "doc_text": "AFP_ENG_19970407.0311\n\nBERLIN, April 7 , 1997 (AFP)\n\nGerman writer Stephan Hermlin dies aged 81\n\n\n\n\nThe controversial German writer Stefan Hermlin died overnight in Berlin at the age of 81, his publisher announced Monday.\n\nHermlin was one of the leading figures of official Communist literature in the former East Germany, and was awarded the National Prize several times by the state.\n\nHe was a Communist militant from his youth, and was active in the struggle against fascism. He also spoke out for East German dissidents like singer and writer Wolf Biermann.\n\nIn 1937, Hermlin emigrated to Palestine, then moved to France in 1940 before moving to Switzerland in 1943.",
